From d27e2f18f31703f01c25d268b46391ad507d9af4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Lucas Garfield (depsolve-perf prototype)" <proto@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:24:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] depsolvednf: let callers choose the package metadata
 level

osbuild-depsolve-dnf V2 learned an optional `package_metadata` request
argument ("full", the default, or "minimal"). Expose it on the Solver
with SetPackageMetadata(), and add AddOptionalMetadata() to load extra
repository metadata types such as "filelists" (which is what makes the
depsolver return per-package file lists on Fedora 40+ and EL10+).

Both are sent with depsolve, dump and search requests. When neither is
set the requests are byte-for-byte identical to before.

manifestgen reads three developer-only IMAGE_BUILDER_EXPERIMENTAL flags
so `image-builder manifest` can exercise these paths without a new CLI
option:

  depsolve-package-metadata=full|minimal
  depsolve-optional-metadata=filelists[+other...]
  depsolve-no-sbom   (skip the depsolver-side SPDX SBOM)

These exist to measure the cost of moving full RPM metadata from the
Python depsolver into image-builder; they are not a supported interface.
