From 7bd6e1557b809a8daac6e4112889da80caa512ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Lucas Garfield (depsolve-perf prototype)" <proto@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:27:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] depsolvednf: add developer-only tracing of depsolver
 round trips

To find out where time goes when the full RPM metadata is moved from
osbuild-depsolve-dnf into image-builder, add opt-in instrumentation:

  IMAGE_BUILDER_DEPSOLVE_TRACE=<file>   append one JSON line per call
  IMAGE_BUILDER_DEPSOLVE_CAPTURE=<dir>  save raw request/response bytes

Each record has the request/response sizes, the time spent marshalling
the request, the depsolver process time (start to exit) with the arrival
time of the first and last stdout byte, json.Unmarshal into the v2 wire
structs, conversion into rpmmd types, SBOM document creation, the rest
of the post-processing, the total, the depsolver's max RSS and CPU time
from rusage, the Go process max RSS and allocation delta, and the field
coverage of the returned packages (computed after the timers stop).

When neither variable is set the helpers are no-ops and run() behaves as
before. While tracing, depsolver calls are serialized.
